Between August 14 and 17, some attempts to connect Quantified Self with ChatGPT failed after a change to ChatGPT’s custom-app authentication flow.

We have resolved the compatibility issue. If your Quantified Self connection is working, you do not need to do anything.

If you could not connect or saw an “invalid_client” message, please recreate your custom app in ChatGPT:

1. Open the existing custom Quantified Self app in ChatGPT and select Manage.
2. Select Delete and confirm. This removes only the custom app from ChatGPT; it does not uninstall ChatGPT itself.
3. Create it again with Quantified Self’s MCP server URL: https://quantified-self.io/mcp
4. Scan the available tools, then sign in to Quantified Self and approve the read-only permissions you want to grant.

Recreating the app makes ChatGPT fetch the current sign-in configuration. No activities, health data, or existing working connections were affected.

Open your MCP connection settings: {{mcp_settings_url}}

If you have a question or still cannot connect, reply to this email. I read every reply personally.

